<title>USA: Central U.S. carlot beef trade 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>Central U.S. carlot beef trade 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cow and bull carcasses not established, according to USDA.</p>
<p>COW &amp; BULL CARCASS CAF WEST COAST  Nil Loads Reported.</p>
<p>			  Lds     Price Range    Latest Estb. Mkt.</p>
<p>UT,brk 2-4 450#/up				  68.00 A</p>
<p>UT,bng 1-3 400#/up				  71.00 - 72.00 A</p>
<p>Cutter 1-2 350#/up				  70.00 D</p>
<p>Bulls YG 1 500#/up				  unq</p>
<p>BONELESS PROCESSING BEEF/BEEF TRIMMINGS  85.0  Loads Reported. Lean boneless beef not established; 85% generally steady; 75% sharply lower compared to last market test; 65% steady to weak. Demand light for moderate offerings. Beef trimmings generally steady on moderate demand and offerings.</p>
<p>FOB OMAHA BASIS:</p>
